.page crc32 1 print the CRC-32 checksum of files

# SYNOPSIS
*crc32* [_FILE_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`crc32` prints the CRC-32 checksum (the one used by zip and PNG) of each _FILE_, followed by the size in bytes and the file name. Standard input is read when there is no file; then the line has no name.

# EXAMPLES
    echo -n abc | crc32
    crc32 /Hakurei/etc/passwd

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if a file could not be read.

# SEE ALSO
md5sum(1), sha256sum(1)
